.SH NAME
fatrat \- download/upload manager for Linux
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B fatrat
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ links
\&...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
This manual page documents briefly the
.B fatrat
command.
.PP
.\" TeX users may be more comfortable with the \fB<whatever>\fP and
.\" \fI<whatever>\fP escape sequences to invode bold face and italics,
.\" respectively.
\fBfatrat\fP is an open source graphical download/upload manager
written in C++ and built on top of the Qt 6 library. It can also run without
a user interface, as a server controlled through its web interface, REST API,
terminal client (\fBfatrat\-tui\fR) or D\-Bus.
.SH OPTIONS
This program follows the usual GNU command line syntax, with long
options starting with two dashes (`-').
A summary of options is included below.
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show summary of options.
.TP
.B \-f, \-\-force
Run the program even if an instance already exists.
.TP
.B \-i, \-\-hidden
Hide the GUI at startup (works only if the tray icon exists).
Only available in the desktop build; \fBfatrat\-nogui\fR and builds without the GUI
do not list this option.
.TP
.B \-n, \-\-nogui
Start with no GUI at all. Useful for running as a daemon.
Only available in the desktop build (running as \fBfatrat\-nogui\fR has the same effect).
.TP
.B \-d, \-\-daemon
Daemonize the application (assumes \fB\-\-nogui\fR).
.TP
.B \-\-rest\-socket \fIpath\fR
Also serve the REST API on a unix socket at \fIpath\fR, whether or not the web
interface is enabled. The socket has mode 0600 and requests on it are not
authenticated, access is governed by file permissions. Only available if built with the web interface.
.TP
.B \-\-syslog
Print global log contents to syslog.
.TP
.B \-p, \-\-pidfile \fIfile\fR
Write the PID to \fIfile\fR. The file is removed on a clean exit.
.TP
.B \-u, \-\-user \fIuser\fR[:\fIgroup\fR]
Drop privileges to \fIuser\fR: the supplementary groups are replaced by those of \fIuser\fR and the group is set to \fIgroup\fR, or to the primary group of \fIuser\fR if not given. The PID file (if any) is handed over to \fIuser\fR and removed on a clean exit.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-python
Disable support for Python extensions. Works only if compiled with extension support.
.TP
.B \-c, \-\-config \fIfile\fR
Use \fIfile\fR (INI format) as settings storage instead of
\fI~/.config/Dolezel/fatrat.conf\fR
.PP
An unknown option is reported and ignored, it does not consume the argument after it.
.PP
If started in the GUI mode, you may pass \fIlinks\fR
as arguments and they will be presented to the user.
.SH WATCH FOLDERS
Each queue can watch a folder. \fB.torrent\fR, \fB.metalink\fR, \fB.meta4\fR,
\fB.txt\fR (one link per line) and \fB.magnet\fR files dropped into it are
added to the queue once they have stopped changing for two seconds. Each
file is then renamed to \fIname\fB.added\fR, or to \fIname\fB.failed\fR if
nothing could be added. Folders are also rescanned every minute, for
network mounts. Set the folder in the queue's properties in the desktop,
web or terminal interface, or through the REST API (\fBwatchDirectory\fR).
